WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:36.870
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.420
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:35.380
The clash between Slifer and Obelisk showed us a vision of our past.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.260
Kaiba, it's fine if you want to deny it.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.980
But for me, I have no future unless I regain my lost memories!

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:49.770
If that vision leads to a certain future, I will seize it!

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:55.030
And I will defeat Kaiba to fulfill my promise with Jonouchi!

00:01:55.030 --> 00:02:01.030
Promise with a Friend
Red-Eyes B. Dragon

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:13.710
That's Obelisk the Tormentor!

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.800
Kaiba summoned his God again?

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.860
Damn!  What is Yugi doing?

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.060
Honda!

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:27.800
Hey, Jonouchi!

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.100
Wake up already and cheer for Yugi!

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:34.080
Don't be absurd!

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.340
Honda!  Stop!

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.200
Honda!

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.440
What are you doing?

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.430
Be quiet!

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.360
He wants to see Yugi's duel!

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.140
Honda...

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:49.280
I'll show it to you!

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.500
Look!  Open your eyes and look, Jonouchi!

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.760
Our Yugi is fighting hard!

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.320
Yugi.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:18.610
Your fixation with that lame illusion is your weakness.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.840
I set a card!

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:25.970
I end my turn.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:33.400
Monster Reborn's effect can only revive my God for one turn.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.090
Return to the earth, Obelisk!

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.820
Yugi, it's no use fighting.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:56.050
I'll destroy you this turn, along with the tablet in my memories!

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:04.150
My future exists when I win this battle!

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.940
My lost memories...

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:15.100
Like Kaiba said, I may only be chasing my past.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:21.000
But I can't move forward until I regain them!

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:25.940
Though it should have lost its power, the Millennium Necklace showed our future.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:30.880
In order for our promise to come true, I can't afford to lose!

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.920
Yugi?

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.520
Where is everyone?

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.260
Sheesh!  Where have you been?

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.600
I searched everywhere!

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.140
Wow, Jonouchi!

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:04.440
You made the final eight!

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:07.900
It's because I'm a good teacher.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:13.250
But even I didn't think you'd make it this far.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.720
Well done!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.060
C'mon now!

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:21.320
Katsuya Jonouchi isn't satisfied by making the final eight!

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.170
I'm going for #1!

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.170
That's the spirit, Jonouchi!

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:27.600
Yeah!

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:31.040
Your hand always has potential.

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:35.320
If you believe that, you may really win the tournament.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:38.410
I "may"?  What's with that!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.220
Start with 2000 life points.  No tributes allowed.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.600
No attacks on the first turn.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.830
Monsters can't attack directly.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.260
Understood?

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:54.980
Yes!

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:55.830
Yeah!

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:10.130
Begin the first quarterfinal match!

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.800
Here I go!  My turn!

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:18.060
I summon Nekogal #1!

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.230
I end my turn!

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.280
Here I go!

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.160
It's my turn!  I draw!

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:30.770
Listen, Jonouchi.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.870
Spell and monster card combinations are important.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:42.160
I'll teach that kid the secrets of dueling.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.100
I summon M-Warrior #1!

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.620
And the spell card, Legendary Sword!

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:07.660
Since M-Warrior #1 is Warrior-Type, it gains 300 attack and defense points!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:12.560
M-Warrior #1 attacks Nekogal #1!

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:26.190
How's that!  I end my turn.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:29.960
That was nothing.  It's my turn.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:30.940
I draw!

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.500
I set a card.

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:36.760
I summon Lesser Dragon!

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:41.340
I end my turn.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:45.300
What?  You're ending your turn without attacking?

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:48.280
You won't be able to beat me like that!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.200
My turn!  I draw!

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:52.380
A man always attacks!

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:56.000
M-Warrior #1 attacks Lesser Dragon!

00:07:57.020 --> 00:07:59.040
I activate my trap card!

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.660
Reinforcements!

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.160
What?

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:09.300
Reinforcements raises my monster's attack points by 500 this turn!

00:08:18.380 --> 00:08:20.100
He beat mine?

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.060
Damn!

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.340
You weren't wary of my trap?

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:27.920
Bro, I bet you only made it this far by luck.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.240
Damn!

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:34.640
I summon Tiger Axe!

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.460
I end my turn.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.960
You're a mess.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:58.450
Who'll be the lucky one that gets to enjoy a living hell when I sacrifice him to the darkness?

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:00.800
Hurry up and end this.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:03.000
I'm tired of waiting.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.890
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:15.680
Yugi, our subconscious created images of the Pharaoh and the priest.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:20.840
I don't care if you think that past is real.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:28.010
I don't care if you think this duel is a recreation from 3,000 years ago.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:36.920
I'll completely destroy everything you believe!

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:42.990
You can only look to the past, so I'll destroy you and the past!

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.160
It's the last turn, Yugi.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:52.920
I switch Lord of D. to defense position.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.440
I activate my spell card!

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.820
The Flute of Summoning Dragon!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.160
The Flute of Summoning Dragon!

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:12.680
When Lord of D. plays this flute, I can summon up to two Dragons from my hand.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:17.290
There's only one kind of Dragon he'll summon!

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.620
Come out, Blue-Eyes White Dragon!

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:36.240
Three Blue-Eyes!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:39.100
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.120
I summon Steel Ogre Grotto #1!

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:49.960
1400 attack points?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:52.630
It's stronger than my Tiger Axe!

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:55.060
Damn.  This is bad.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.020
Bro, your skill level's low.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:01.500
I'll never make such a simple attack.

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:04.120
I activate my spell card!

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.080
Polymerization!

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:12.080
I fuse Steel Ogre Grotto #1 and Lesser Dragon to summon Metal Dragon!

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:17.960
Metal Dragon attacks Tiger Axe!

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:24.850
Damn!  My life points!

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:27.120
I end my turn!

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:28.830
It's your turn.

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:32.120
I-I know!  You don't need to tell me!

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.670
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.100
Flame Swordsman.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:40.540
It has 1800 attack points.  Damn.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:44.480
50 attack points less than Metal Dragon.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:48.150
All I can do is survive by using a monster in defense.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.860
I summon Hero of the East in defense position!

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.160
I end my turn!

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:30.690
I have four monsters on my field.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:36.370
Yugi, you only have Dark Magician and a useless monster.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:43.020
You won't survive my monsters' all-out attack this turn!

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.070
Yugi!  You lose!

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:51.160
Even Yugi can't turn this around.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.190
My brother will win this duel!

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:02.440
I wonder who's winning.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:06.180
No matter who wins, I don't want any more casualties.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.380
Don't worry.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:12.760
Since Yugi and Kaiba are dueling, they're playing fair.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.340
I'm rooting for Yugi.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.660
So is he.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.230
My turn!

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:20.200
I draw!

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.500
You won't get away, bro!

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.550
The spell card, Stop Defense!

00:13:24.550 --> 00:13:25.400
What?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:30.020
Stop Defense switches Hero of the East to attack position.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:37.090
Metal Dragon attacks Hero of the East!

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.370
I'm in trouble!

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:46.440
I only have 300 life points left.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:51.070
I set a card and end my turn.

00:13:51.070 --> 00:13:53.000
Listen up, bro.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.410
You're like a candle in the wind.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.600
Be quiet!  It's my turn!

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:58.680
I draw!

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.420
Shield & Sword.

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:08.750
This card swaps all monsters' attack and defense points.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:20.650
I can destroy Metal Dragon if I have a monster with higher defense points.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:26.740
No good.  I don't have that kind of monster in my hand.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:30.700
Just give up, bro.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:34.600
There's no way you can make a comeback.

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:36.920
Is it over?

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:40.220
Your hand always has potential.

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:44.320
Gust Fan!

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:52.680
With this Equip Spell, a Wind Attribute monster gains 400 attack points and loses 200 defense points.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:54.520
I got it!

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.470
Here I go!

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:58.400
I summon Flame Swordsman!

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:04.360
Metal Dragon is a Wind Attribute monster, right?

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:05.380
Yeah.

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:10.440
I equip the spell card Gust Fan on Metal Dragon!

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:18.300
What are you doing?

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:23.700
Gust Fan is an Equip Spell to raise your own monster's attack points.

00:15:23.960 --> 00:15:31.240
It's suicidal to equip it on my Metal Dragon and raise its attack points.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.820
Play seriously!

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:36.200
I am serious.  Super serious!

00:15:36.420 --> 00:15:38.280
I activate my spell card!

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:41.000
Shield & Sword!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:47.640
Shield & Sword swaps attack and defense points!

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:50.740
Metal Dragon's attack points become 1500!

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.730
Flame Swordsman has 1600!

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:55.400
You had that combo?

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.130
Go, Flame Swordsman!

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.930
Attack Metal Dragon!

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.440
All right!  Metal Dragon is destro-

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:08.570
What?

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:10.840
Flame Swordsman is destroyed?

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:12.010
What's going on?

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:19.550
Before you activated Shield & Sword, I activated my trap.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.260
A trap?

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:27.040
Castle Walls raised Metal Dragon's defense points by 500 for a turn.

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:33.630
So when Shield & Sword swapped its attack and defense points...

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:40.840
Yeah.  Flame Swordsman's 1600 attack points vs Metal Dragon's 2000 attack points.

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:48.080
I take the difference as damage - 400 points.

00:16:48.080 --> 00:16:49.480
That means...

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:51.980
The duel is over!

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:53.420
All right!

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:58.570
I lost.  But I did my best.

00:16:58.570 --> 00:17:00.020
I have no regrets.

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:02.560
I lost.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:04.470
Good luck in the semifinals!

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:06.920
Yeah.  Thank you, bro!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:11.870
No one else could come up with that unexpected combo!

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:13.670
You're incredible, bro!

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:15.710
Sorry I said your skill level's low.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.150
It's fine.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:19.150
See ya!

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:21.580
Will you duel me again?

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:25.520
Sure.  But I'll win next time!

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.400
Prepare yourself, Yugi!

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:43.110
And engrave my name in your memories as the true champion!

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:52.850
Like Kaiba says, my Dark Magician and Beta The Magnet Warrior...

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:56.950
...aren't enough to stop three Blue-Eyes' attacks.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:00.120
Seems we have a winner.

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:04.560
The first to be sacrificed to the darkness will be Seto Kaiba.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:08.900
Three Blue-Eyes attack!

00:18:14.060 --> 00:18:16.770
Is this the end for me?

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:19.420
Don't lose, Yugi.

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.550
Jonouchi.

00:18:24.550 --> 00:18:30.180
You told me that your hand always has potential.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:31.620
My hand!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:33.560
Don't give up, Yugi.

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.660
A true duelist never gives up.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:39.040
I see!

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:44.760
You have no hope!  This destructive light sends you to the dark, Yu-

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:45.930
What?

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.170
Red-Eyes?

00:18:51.170 --> 00:18:56.940
The Flute of Summoning Dragon's effect Special Summons Dragons from the hand.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:01.110
That effect doesn't only work for you!

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:06.220
I had Red-Eyes B. Dragon in my hand!

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:09.760
Jonouchi gave me his precious card!

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:20.070
You had that card in your hand?

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:24.230
Sheesh.  Your endgame is weak, Kaiba.

00:19:25.800 --> 00:19:29.960
My Blue-Eyes will destroy you, along with Red-Eyes!

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:32.330
Perish!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:35.400
Triple Burst Stream of Destruction!

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.960
The first target is Dark Magician!

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.970
I activate my trap card!

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:44.290
Magician's Selection!

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:47.760
Magician's Selection?

00:19:47.760 --> 00:19:50.540
When there's a Spellcaster on your field...

00:19:50.540 --> 00:19:53.470
...the trap activates when my monster attacks!

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:55.630
It negates your attack!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:59.810
And your monster with the fewest attack points is destroyed!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.680
But you can't avoid the second and third attacks!

00:20:08.820 --> 00:20:11.120
Beta The Magnet Warrior is destroyed!

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:15.150
Vanish, Jonouchi's ghost!

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:17.290
You'll never destroy his soul!

00:20:17.290 --> 00:20:19.500
I activate my trap!

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:22.060
Spellbinding Circle!

00:20:22.060 --> 00:20:28.520
Spellbinding Circle negates your monster's attack and lowers its attack points by 700!

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:34.410
Red-Eyes counterattacks!

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:39.960
Black Fireball!

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.570
Blue-Eyes is destroyed!

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:52.870
How dare you!  Jonouchi's ghost destroyed my Blue-Eyes!

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:58.200
Jonouchi, you helped me.

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.900
Thank you.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:02.900
Win, Yugi!

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:05.200
Yeah.

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:11.970
Brother!

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:14.080
Jonouchi!

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:31.940
Red-Eyes messed up my plans a bit, but I'm still going to win!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:34.670
He still has two Blue-Eyes.

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:38.450
My memories...  My promise with my friend...

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:42.570
I will win to achieve them!

00:21:54.920 --> 00:22:01.760
Thanks to Jonouchi's Red-Eyes, Yugi survived three Blue-Eyes' attacks.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:06.520
By summoning Red-Eyes, Jonouchi has woken up!

00:22:06.520 --> 00:22:10.870
We're happy, and Jonouchi leaves to cheer for Yugi.

00:22:10.870 --> 00:22:15.410
Yugi and Kaiba's duel is reaching the climax!

00:22:15.570 --> 00:22:18.920
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Fire at Hatred!
Dark Paladin

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:20.470
Duel, standby!

00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:38.510
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:39.010 --> 00:22:46.850
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:48.580 --> 00:22:58.010
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:07.540
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:23:08.100 --> 00:23:16.560
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:22.070
I'll live feeling them

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:27.260
For me to be me

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:35.710
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:41.350
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:41.870 --> 00:23:51.010
We'll both understand that someday
